applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ODA, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTSU, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARAI TORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA MASATAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAOE TAKANORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHITOBA YUKIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ODA TAKESHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OTSU TOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, TORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA, MASATAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAOE, TAKANORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHITOBA, YUKIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ODA, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTSU, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An ethylene/aromatic vinyl copolymer characterized by satisfying the following: (1) It has an aromatic vinyl content of 0.5 to 10 mol%; (2) It gives a 0.2 mm-thick molding which has a haze of 14% or lower or a total light transmittance of 90 % or higher; (3) It satisfies the following relationship (1) between the aromatic vinyl content and the glass transition point (Tg) which is determined by the inflection point method and is observed with a differential scanning calorimeter (DSC) at temperatures not lower than -50  DEG C: -20 + 1.00St &gt; Tg &gt; -30 + 1.05St relationship (1) wherein St represents the aromatic vinyl content of the copolymer (mol%); (4) It has a weight-average molecular weight of 140,000 to 500,000 when the aromatic vinyl content is 5 to 10 mol%, and of 60,000 to 500,000 when the aromatic vinyl content is 0.5 to 5 mol%, excluding 5 mol%.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un copolymère d'éthylène/vinyle aromatique caractérisé par le fait qu'il remplit les conditions suivantes: (1) il présente une teneur en vinyle aromatique de 0,5 à 10 mol %, (2) il donne un moulage d'une épaisseur de 0,2 mm ayant un voile de 14 % ou moins ou bien un facteur de transmission totale de lumière de 90 % ou davantage, (3) il satisfait la relation (1)-20 + 1,00St &gt; Tg &gt; -30 + 1,05St entre la teneur en vinyle aromatique et le point de transition vitreuse (Tg), lequel est déterminé par la méthode du point d'inflexion et est observé avec un calorimètre à balayage différentiel (DSC) à des températures non inférieures à 0  DEG C, relation dans laquelle St représente la teneur en vinyle aromatique du copolymère (mol %), (4) il présente un poids moléculaire moyen au poids de 140000 à 500000 lorsque la teneur en vinyle aromatique est comprise entre 5 et 10 mol %, et de 60000 à 500000 lorsque la teneur en vinyle aromatique est comprise entre 0,5 et 5md %, 5 mol % exclu.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>